 " is the search."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"d435ccb8-76dd-4b2a-ba23-c89c4d40b9e6"],

Cell["\<\
Definition: a line is an inextensible geodesic \[LongDash] a shortest path \
that no neighbour of either end prolongs.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"cf5f5e2b-4e73-4b86-8deb-bb1e033dc869"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its graph \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMeasurement"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMeasurement", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["g", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["line", "TI"], ",", " ", "\"\<Graph\>\""}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79169d03-79cf-4f0e-b494-199e9acebca3"],
 " \[LongDash] is a ",
 Cell[BoxData["List"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7f896aa-f9f0-4df4-8868-29b91c8b795d"],
 " of DAGs, one per pair of ends (",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ") that is compatible, ",
 StyleBox["d(a, b) = d(a, p) + d(p, q) + d(q, b)", "TI"],
 ", and maximal, no neighbour of ",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 " lengthening ",
 StyleBox["d(a, b)", "TI"],
 ". The DAG for (",
 StyleBox["a", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["b", "TI"],
 ") is the union of the intervals ",
 StyleBox["I(a, p)", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["I(p, q)", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["I(q, b)", "TI"],
 ". Its chains are exactly the lines with those ends, and every line is a \
chain of exactly one DAG, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Faithful\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e76e2eb2-9655-4938-94e8-e6611ba40475"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "931d466b-1829-4ac7-a52a-ddbec14618b0"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6b032f1c-ab6a-449f-affe-4acdec6fe97f"],

Cell["\<\
The list is not optional. The union of the DAGs can carry chains that are not \
geodesics: through the edge 1\[Dash]2 of the 6-cycle there are three DAGs and \
three lines, while their union would add a fourth path that is not a geodesic.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f029b3b6-d565-4cc2-9285-f4bb8f003506"],

Cell["\<\
The DAGs are alternatives, so the counts add across them. The family can be \
astronomical while the list stays small.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f7d05f6c-e9f3-4fb5-81f9-664713aa7132"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " = ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraLine"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraLine", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37344c7d-bf6e-4546-9270-6955d9bdfbda"],
 " is every maximal geodesic through ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 ", once per orientation."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0d75c0a5-13d4-45ad-baab-4635c04484de"]
}, Open  ]],

